    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0776" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1946v06/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">361.1121/6–1846: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-18">June 18, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received July 2—9:52
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–313. Reference Department’s airgrams A–122, March 20, 1946 and A–175, May 7,
                        1946<anchor n="6" xml:id="d516-f1"/> regarding Mr. Isaiah Oggins, an
                    American citizen imprisoned by the Soviet authorities several years ago.<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d516-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0777" n="763" xml:id="pg763"/>
                <p>The Embassy addressed a note to the Soviet Ministry of Foreign Affairs on March
                    30, 1946 on this subject but has thus far received no reply. A new note covering
                    the points in the latter reference airgram is being sent today, and the Embassy
                    will inform the Department as soon as it receives a reply.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d516-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d516-f1" n="6" xml:id="d516-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d516-f2" n="7" xml:id="d516-f2-content">
                <p>For the origin of this case, see <ref target="frus1942v03#pg_765"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 765</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1942v03#pg_771">771</ref>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">passim</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d516-f3" n="8" xml:id="d516-f3-content">
                <p>Mrs. Oggins was informed by letter on July 22 of these latest inquiries made by
                    the Embassy at Moscow concerning her husband. There were no further developments
                    to report during 1946.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
